From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:23:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] cheetah: install SCONE and Tycho, as stock does

vendor/gms defines SCONE-v77459 and Tycho, but gms_full.mk installs them only
when PRODUCT_MANUFACTURER is Google, which it isn't yet while the product
makefiles are inherited. Play services then updated the missing SCONE as a
user app, which crashed after boot without its privileged permissions
(WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS). Same as kodiak's device.mk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 device-cheetah.mk | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device-cheetah.mk b/device-cheetah.mk
index 8efbfdd..a36721e 100644
--- a/device-cheetah.mk
+++ b/device-cheetah.mk
@@ -72,3 +72,11 @@ DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE += \
     $(DEVICE_PATH)/vintf/manifest.xml
 DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE += \
     $(DEVICE_PATH)/vintf/device_framework_matrix_product.xml
+
+# Adaptive Connectivity Services (SCONE) and Google Fi (Tycho): vendor/gms
+# defines both, but gms_full.mk's PRODUCT_MANUFACTURER filter doesn't match
+# inside inherit-product, so neither was installed. SCONE's privileged
+# permission allowlist already ships (privapp-permissions-google-p*.xml).
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    SCONE-v77459 \
+    Tycho
